{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "edbce5eb36",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# A complete 50 mA SKY130 LDO with a local gate feedback loop\n",
    "\n",
    "**Christian Reivan**  \n",
    "**GitHub: [christianreivan](https://github.com/christianreivan)**  \n",
    "SSCS Code a Chip submission for ISSCC 2027\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook implements a complete transistor LDO in SKY130. A current mirror\n",
    "error amplifier controls a PMOS super source follower, which drives an NMOS pass\n",
    "array. A physical bias circuit, direct output feedback, compensation, and an\n",
    "output bleeder complete the regulator. The voltage reference is supplied externally.\n",
    "\n",
    "The circuit regulates 1.2 V to 1.0 V for loads from 0 to 50 mA. The amplifier and\n",
    "driver use a separate 1.8 V supply. At TT and 27 °C with a 100 pF output capacitor,\n",
    "native ngspice simulation gives 1.0009 V at zero load and 1.0001 V at 50 mA.\n",
    "Both supply ports are measured independently, because good rejection of VIN does\n",
    "not establish good rejection of the driver supply.\n",
    "\n",
    "The design exercise follows the entire path from transistor bias to closed loop\n",
    "behavior. It shows why a larger output capacitor can improve ripple attenuation\n",
    "while reducing the phase margin at light load, why the gate driver needs its own\n",
    "supply rejection analysis, and why an LDO can regulate accurately yet respond\n",
    "poorly to a large, fast load step.\n",
    "\n",
    "The notebook includes the complete circuit, transistor dimensions, native simulation\n",
    "decks, public compact models, and executable analysis. Results are circuit\n",
    "simulations. Layout, extracted interconnect, device mismatch, and silicon\n",
    "measurements are outside the present implementation.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0a79e029ef",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Circuit and operating conditions\n",
    "\n",
    "The regulated power path is VIN → NPASS → VOUT. The amplifier compares VOUT with\n",
    "VREF and produces EA. The local driver controls GATE through PF and PUP. BN biases\n",
    "the amplifier and driver current sinks. Named nets connect the four transistor\n",
    "sheets below, and the complete SPICE deck contains all of them together.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Quantity | Value |\n",
    "| :--- | :--- |\n",
    "| Power input VIN | 1.2 V nominal |\n",
    "| Amplifier and driver supply VAA | 1.8 V |\n",
    "| External reference VREF | 1.0 V |\n",
    "| Regulated output | 1.0 V |\n",
    "| Load current | 0 to 50 mA |\n",
    "| Output capacitor | 10, 50, 100, and 350 pF |\n",
    "| Nominal output capacitor | 100 pF |\n",
    "| Other intentional capacitance | 201.618 pF |\n",
    "| Output bleeder | 100 kΩ |\n",
    "| Nominal process and temperature | SKY130 TT, 27 °C |\n",
    "\n",
    "NPASS has its body connected to VOUT. The circuit therefore assumes an isolated\n",
    "NFET body. A physical implementation must provide the required well isolation\n",
    "and recheck junction bias and parasitic coupling. The large pass array uses\n",
    "2400 parallel units, each with W = 5 µm and L = 0.15 µm. Total width is 12 mm.\n",
    "This width is not a layout area estimate.\n",
    "\n",
    "The load is an independent current source. Its incremental resistance is infinite.\n",
    "The small signal analysis must therefore retain the 100 kΩ bleeder, rather than\n",
    "replace the load with the ratio VOUT/ILOAD.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "adf91503bd",
