      "text/plain": [
       "                                       Value\n",
       "Amplifier gm (mS)                     1.8964\n",
       "Amplifier output resistance (kΩ)    249.1642\n",
       "BU impedance (kΩ)                     7.5183\n",
       "Driver DC gain                        0.9735\n",
       "Pass DC gain                          0.9196\n",
       "Hand precision gain (dB)             52.5272\n",
       "Native precision gain at 1 Hz (dB)   52.8128"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "devices = op.set_index('name')\n",
    "gm = lambda name: float(devices.loc[name, 'gm'])\n",
    "ro = lambda name: float(devices.loc[name, 'ro_ohm'])\n",
    "gm_ea = gm('n1l') * gm('p4l') / (gm('p3l') - gm('p2l') + 1/ro('n1l') + 1/ro('p2l') + 1/ro('p3l'))\n",
    "re = 1 / (1/ro('p4r') + 1/ro('n5r'))\n",
    "zbu = 1 / (gm('pbr') + 1/ro('pbr') + 1/ro('nbr'))\n",
    "zh = 1 / (1/ro('pf') + 1/ro('nlim') + 1/(1000 + zbu))\n",
    "zd = 1 / (gm('pf') + 1/ro('pf') + 1/ro('pup')\n",
    "          + (gm('pup') - 1/ro('pf')) * (gm('pf') + 1/ro('pf')) * zh)\n",
    "driver_gain = zd * gm('pf') * (1 + (gm('pup') - 1/ro('pf')) * zh)\n",
    "pass_gain = gm('pass') / (gm('pass') + 1/ro('pass') + 1/100000)\n",
    "hand_gain_db = 20*np.log10(gm_ea * re * driver_gain * pass_gain)\n",
    "native_gain_db = float(lab.loop_response(CASE, DATA).magnitude_db.iloc[0])\n",
    "display(pd.Series({'Amplifier gm (mS)':gm_ea*1e3, 'Amplifier output resistance (kΩ)':re/1000,\n",
    "                   'BU impedance (kΩ)':zbu/1000, 'Driver DC gain':driver_gain,\n",
    "                   'Pass DC gain':pass_gain, 'Hand precision gain (dB)':hand_gain_db,\n",
    "                   'Native precision gain at 1 Hz (dB)':native_gain_db}).round(4).to_frame('Value'))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "57b59804c7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Supply rejection across frequency\n",
    "\n",
    "Here PSR is $20\\log_{10}|v_o/v_{\\mathrm{supply}}|$, so a more negative value means\n",
    "better rejection. Each source is excited separately while the other ideal voltage\n",
    "sources are AC quiet. Both supply curves span 1 Hz to 1 GHz with the complete\n",
    "compact model terminal charges enabled.\n",
    "\n",
    "The low frequency precision gain suppresses both supply paths. Rejection weakens\n",
    "as that gain falls and the driver and pass paths become dominant. The driver supply\n",
    "curve must be evaluated separately from VIN.\n"
   ]
  },
