  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "307803742b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 10. Output capacitor and loop dynamics\n",
    "\n",
    "The same transistor dimensions and compensation are used at every output\n",
    "capacitance. At zero external load, increasing COUT improves high frequency VIN\n",
    "attenuation but lowers the output pole and reduces the precision loop phase margin estimate.\n",
    "At 50 mA the pass transconductance is much larger, so the output node behaves differently.\n"
   ]
  },
