  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "504d6dc8a8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The precision loop test inserts a zero DC voltage source between VOUT and VFB.\n",
    "An AC excitation of that source gives the voltage injection estimate\n",
    "$T_v=-v_o/v_{FB}$. Separate port tests open the VOUT to VFB connection, hold VFB\n",
    "at its connected DC voltage, and measure the VFB input impedance and VOUT output\n",
    "impedance. These differ from closed loop output impedance and from VIN input\n",
    "impedance. Around crossover, their magnitude ratio\n",
    "exceeds 2600 in the least favorable tested nominal case. This supports the voltage\n",
    "injection approximation at that boundary.\n",
    "\n",
    "The following curves are precision loop estimates with the local driver still\n",
    "connected. They are not a product of two independently measured closed loops.\n",
    "Small load step responses provide an additional check on the connected dynamics.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "be3644444b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1320x840 with 4 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(11, 7), sharex=True, constrained_layout=True)\n",
    "for row, load in enumerate((0,50)):\n",
    "    for cap in (10,50,100,350):\n",
    "        curve = lab.loop_response(f'tied_load{load}mA_cout{cap}pF', DATA)\n",
    "        axes[row,0].semilogx(curve.frequency_hz, curve.magnitude_db, label=f'{cap} pF')\n",
    "        axes[row,1].semilogx(curve.frequency_hz, curve.phase_deg, label=f'{cap} pF')\n",
    "    axes[row,0].set(title=f'Precision loop, {load} mA', ylabel='Magnitude (dB)', ylim=(-60,70))\n",
    "    axes[row,1].set(title=f'Precision loop phase, {load} mA', ylabel='Phase (degrees)', ylim=(-270,20))\n",
    "    axes[row,0].axhline(0, color='grey', lw=.8)\n",
    "    axes[row,1].axhline(-180, color='grey', lw=.8)\n",
    "for axis in axes.flat:\n",
    "    axis.set_xlim(1e3,1e8)\n",
    "    axis.grid(alpha=.25)\n",
    "for axis in axes[-1]:\n",
    "    axis.set_xlabel('Frequency (Hz)')\n",
    "axes[0,0].legend(ncol=2)\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "78ad7e3eeb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 11. Closed loop output impedance and reference transfer\n",
    "\n",
    "The load source injects a small AC current into the connected regulator. Since\n",
    "positive load current removes charge, $Z_{\\mathrm{OUT}}=-v_o/i_L$.\n",
    "This is the closed loop output impedance. The precision loop and local driver\n",
    "remain connected throughout the measurement.\n",
    "\n",
    "The reference response includes the common external source that drives both N1R\n",
    "and NPROGRAM. Its extra bias path explains why the exact reference response need\n",
    "not equal $T/(1+T)$.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "fd963c8eee",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1320x480 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(11, 4), constrained_layout=True)\n",
    "for load in (0,50):\n",
    "    for cap in (10,100,350):\n",
    "        curve = lab.output_impedance(f'tied_load{load}mA_cout{cap}pF', DATA)\n",
    "        axes[0].loglog(curve.frequency_hz, curve.magnitude, label=f'{load} mA, {cap} pF')\n",
    "    ref = lab.reference(f'tied_load{load}mA_cout100pF', DATA)\n",
    "    axes[1].semilogx(ref.frequency_hz, ref.magnitude_db, label=f'{load} mA')\n",
    "axes[0].set(title='Closed loop output impedance', ylabel='Impedance (Ω)')\n",
    "axes[1].set(title='Shared reference transfer, 100 pF', ylabel='Reference transfer (dB)')\n",
    "for axis in axes:\n",
    "    axis.set(xlabel='Frequency (Hz)', xlim=(1,1e9))\n",
    "    axis.grid(alpha=.25)\n",
    "    axis.legend(fontsize=8)\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7147eda872",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 12. Process and temperature\n",
    "\n",
    "The sweep covers TT, SS, FF, SF, and FS at 0, 27, and 85 °C. Each condition is\n",
    "tested at zero and 50 mA with 100 pF, VIN = 1.2 V, and VAA = 1.8 V. The curves\n",
    "below show the envelope of the 30 native responses. This is a process and\n",
    "temperature sweep at fixed supply voltages, rather than a mismatch analysis.\n",
    "\n",
    "Accurate DC regulation does not guarantee good supply rejection. The weakest\n",
    "driver supply condition has only about 3.6 dB of attenuation even though its DC\n",
    "output is close to the reference. This is a concrete reason to characterize VAA.\n"
   ]
  },
