   "source": [
    "## 13. Small load steps and the loop injection boundary\n",
    "\n",
    "The small load excursion is 0.1 µA at zero external load and 50 µA around 50 mA.\n",
    "The load rises at 2 µs and returns at 7 µs with 10 ns edges. The graphs divide\n",
    "the output excursion by the corresponding current step so their scales are\n",
    "comparable. This is a time domain load response, not a second frequency domain\n",
    "output impedance measurement.\n",
    "\n",
    "All eight cases return toward their initial operating point. Ringing is most\n",
    "pronounced at zero load with 350 pF, consistent with its smaller phase margin\n",
    "estimate. The table reports the independently measured impedance ratio around\n",
    "each crossover used to assess the voltage injection boundary.\n"
   ]
  },
