   "id": "82b38d5fd6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 14. Large load steps\n",
    "\n",
    "A large step tests available charge and current as well as linear loop stability.\n",
    "The load changes from 0 to 50 mA and back with 10 ns edges. COUT alone cannot\n",
    "supply that step for long. If COUT alone supplied the initial current deficit,\n",
    "the slope would be $dv_o/dt=-\\Delta I/C_{\\mathrm{OUT}}$. The actual source node\n",
    "also stores charge in the pass terminal capacitances.\n",
    "\n",
    "The finite driver current and pass gate charge produce approximately 362 to 365 mV\n",
    "undershoot in these tests. Release overshoot is approximately 194 to 198 mV.\n",
    "Increasing COUT within this range does not solve the charging delay of the\n",
    "pass gate. The 350 pF case also takes longer to recover after load release.\n",
    "These results make the design unsuitable for an application requiring small\n",
    "voltage excursions during this particular full scale step.\n",
    "\n",
    "The plots show both VOUT and GATE so the gate motion can be examined alongside\n",
    "the output error. The native maximum time step is 0.5 ns. A separate 0.25 ns\n",
    "check at 100 pF changes undershoot by less than 0.01 mV.\n"
   ]
  },
