  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d719a989d5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 17. Reproduce and extend\n",
    "\n",
    "Set `RUN_NATIVE = True` near the beginning to regenerate the complete experiment.\n",
    "The notebook then uses the new results for every plot and table. A terminal run\n",
    "can perform the same experiment:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "python scripts/ldo_lab.py regenerate --all-cases --output work/full_run\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "The canonical transistor circuit is in `circuits/ldo.spice` and `circuits/ldo.json`.\n",
    "Each case includes its own complete testbench. The native runner substitutes the\n",
    "public model library path, sets the required SKY130 simulator compatibility, and\n",
    "preserves the input deck and raw output in the new directory. It refuses to replace\n",
    "an existing populated run directory.\n",
    "\n",
    "Useful extensions are to change CR and compare both supplies, rescale CGATE and\n",
    "CEA together with the real driver, or change the minimum bleed current and repeat\n",
    "the zero load checks. A change is successful only if DC regulation, supply\n",
    "transfer, gate headroom, and connected dynamics remain satisfactory together.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fc3803ff38",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Design interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "The complete circuit separates precision regulation from local gate drive. The\n",
    "outer amplifier provides high low frequency gain. The local PF and PUP loop\n",
    "controls the large pass gate capacitance. Both loops depend on the real bias\n",
    "impedances, available headroom, and transistor operating points.\n",
    "\n",
    "The low frequency supply transfer is much smaller than the peak near the driver\n",
    "bandwidth. When the precision gain falls, the finite pass output resistance and\n",
    "capacitive paths become visible. With the pass gate quiet, the low frequency\n",
    "pass contribution alone approaches\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{1/r_{oP}}{g_{mP}+1/r_{oP}+1/R_{\\mathrm{BLEED}}},\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "which is approximately 0.0804 at 50 mA. The connected driver changes this result,\n",
    "but a quiet gate by itself does not eliminate the finite output resistance path.\n",
    "\n",
    "The capacitor sweep also prevents a misleading single condition conclusion.\n",
    "Increasing COUT helps some ripple paths yet lowers the light load output pole.\n",
    "At 350 pF the nominal zero load phase margin estimate is approximately 24°.\n",
    "That condition has less damping than the 100 pF nominal design and requires\n",
    "additional compensation before use in an application that needs a larger margin.\n",
    "\n",
    "This implementation is a complete simulation design for studying these tradeoffs.\n",
    "Its next physical design steps are isolated body implementation, pass array layout,\n",
    "capacitor area estimation, interconnect extraction, mismatch evaluation, and\n",
    "verification with realistic reference and auxiliary supply impedances.\n"
   ]
  },
